{
  "about": "Swiss German / German church vocabulary for the sermon translator. Used three ways: (1) glossary for the LLM translator, (2) custom-vocabulary / keyword hints for speech-to-text engines that accept them, (3) a checklist when scoring the bake-off.",
  "notes": [
    "Swiss German has no standard spelling. The 'gsw' forms are approximate spellings of how the word may sound (mostly Zürich/Bern style). They are hints, not a dictionary. Correct them after hearing the real speaker.",
    "Most speech engines write Standard German even when they hear dialect, so 'de' is the form the translator will usually see.",
    "'en' is the preferred English. Names of GOD are in capitals and His titles and pronouns are capitalised, by the owner's preference.",
    "Entries with 'trap' are words a general translator often gets wrong in a church context."
  ],
